      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62393928546a41082c280c5b|full_name}: good to know about the vibration. I just hope we'll be able to turn it all off soon. \nThe interaction graphical elements are just a bit overkill. I personally don't need a blue outline, transparent blue fill, and a dashed line rendering over everything to know I can pickup a mug. A mod used to exist that changed it to just a outline and nothing else and that alone was much better but being able to turn it off would be amazing. \nSame goes for stations I guess but I didn't elaborate on that directly. \nWith the addition of options to disable the hud or enable an \"immersive\" mode, I'd expect all these graphical elements to get hidden even if they aren't necessarily hud elements. Anything that renders over world elements and is part of my vision id expect to be able to disable. I'm not Master Chief. I'm a 3 foot tall bunny. I don't need AI vision. Especially not after 20k hours. \nI felt like this was just an opportune moment to bring this up and I'm sure it will eventually be addressed but this seemed like the best opportunity to do so. Fingers crossed!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
