  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since 2017 I've been waiting for a method to disable pickup interactions. Always thought it was a mild oversight that would be rectified in the next big menu update. Yet it doesn't seem to have been added in this one. \nRequest: Slider to adjust the opacity of the pickup interactions (outline, dashed line). And a method to disable the vibration. \nWhy?: The ability to adjust HUD elements is awesome. Being able to disable specific parts of the HUD or disable the HUD entirely is a good thing. I personally play with my HUD off and nameplates off. I find it more immersive. But nothing rips me out of that immersion more than seeing all these blue pickup interactions in my face constantly. It's obnoxious especially when there are multiple pickups all right next to each other. Disabling the HUD should disable the HUD. Not leave elements that can't be disabled no matter what, especially when they're as intrusive as the pickup interactions. \nWatching the new video regarding the main menu I got the feeling they want to give users more control. So this oversight seems even more silly. \nSummary: please add a method to disable pickup interactions so we can finally turn off the entire HUD should we choose to. Thanks.",
